  },
  {
    "episode_id": 72487,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72487.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 119,
    "turn_text": "Right, I think that that is the question that a lot of folks, not only in the Democratic Party, but the Republican Party are also privately questioning here. What are the intentions of this group? It's not clear. Their donors are private, so we don't know who is really financing this $70 million operation. And no labels, they say that they are not for sure even putting forward a ticket. but instead that they're leaving the door open, especially in the scenario where to be a Trump Biden rematch. And though we should know, though, Tom, we've talked to a great many voters who said they would like a third option. And here in the American Democratic system, we've become accustomed to a two-party system over the last 100 years, but it doesn't mean that it has to remain that way.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_17",
